# scripts/magiccheck.sh: engine files allowed to name the game, and why.
# <file under src/> <literal as reported, without spaces | *> <reason>
#
# The exe's own tables as the rules' built-in rows (rules-dump writes them, an OpenGorky
# project's rules files override them). They are the Classic reader's rows but cannot move
# to core/classic.zig: rules.zig -> core/classic.zig -> core/behaviour.zig -> rules.zig is a
# file cycle (scripts/deps.py).
rules/ai.zig * the exe's AI profile table 0x4bcbb0 (rules AiProfile built-ins)
rules/attacks.zig * the exe's attack branches by classic_id (rules MonsterAttack, HeroAttack, WdelayHero built-ins)
rules/campaign.zig * the exe's new game 0x413386 (rules Campaign built-in)
rules/party.zig * the exe's idle chatter and hidden weapons by hero (rules IdleChatter, HiddenWeapons built-ins)
rules/resist.zig * the exe's resistance table by classic_id (rules Resist built-ins)
rules/ui.zig * the exe's kill and skill icons by classic_id (rules KillIcon, SkillIcon built-ins)
# Not the engine's behaviour.
game/scene_check.zig * the scene checker (gorky-tool): joiner heroes and their levels, a dev tool
viewer/battle/gui.zig "Victory" the banner's fallback text when string.tab has no 501
viewer/menu.zig "01_credits_" the credits fonts' file names (asset names)
